## Agent File Integrity

**Agents and the orchestrator must never create, modify, or delete agent infrastructure files during sprint work or any other workflow.**

Protected paths — read-only for all agents and the orchestrator at all times:

| Path | Contents |
|---|---|
| `{RUNTIME_ROOT}/*_instructions.md` | Role instruction files |
| `.mt-agent-devkit/rules/` | All rules files |
| `.mt-agent-devkit/workflows/` | All workflow files |
| `.mt-agent-devkit/context/` | Project priming and document index |
| `{RUNTIME_ROOT}/devkit_version.txt` | Installed devkit version stamp |
| `.mt-agent-devkit/instructions/orchestrator_instructions.md` | Orchestrator-only routing, session-management, and completion-report reference |

Writable paths during normal work:

| Path | Who writes | What |
|---|---|---|
| `{RUNTIME_ROOT}/memory/` | Each agent | Their own memory file only |
| `{RUNTIME_ROOT}/working-record/` | Each agent | Their own working record only |
| `{RUNTIME_ROOT}/tmp/` | Orchestrator | Pipeline state files |
| `{RUNTIME_ROOT}/docs/` | All agents | Stories, sprints, reviews (strict mode only) |

**The only operation that may update protected paths is `sync devkit`**, which is triggered explicitly by the user and handled exclusively by `Sync_Devkit_Workflow.md`. No agent, no workflow, and no orchestrator logic may modify these files for any other reason — including fixes, improvements, or adjustments discovered during sprint work.

If an agent identifies an error or improvement needed in a rules or workflow file, it must report it to the user as an observation — never self-correct by editing the file.

**Audit carve-out.** `sync devkit` and `update project` (the devkit-side command that applies local templates to this project) may each run a scoped, detect-only audit pass as their own final stage — this is a **workflow step, not an agent role or a third writer of protected paths**. The audit pass never writes to `rules/`, `instructions/`, or `{ENTRYPOINT}` itself; it only reads the files that same run just wrote and, if it finds mode-adaptation drift, files a report Issue on the devkit repository — the fix, if any, lands upstream in `templates/`, never as a local edit here. No other workflow may invoke this audit pass.

